# Jira Comment Signature

Use when writing any Jira comment as part of SmartFlow-authored work.

End every automatically created Jira comment with its own last line: `– erstellt mit SmartFlow`.

## Rules

- Applies to every comment the agent creates or edits over `jira_add_comment` and `jira_edit_comment`: solution comments, transition and occurrence notes, and worklog comments.
- The signature is a separate last line after the comment body, exactly `– erstellt mit SmartFlow`.
- Never append it twice: when editing a comment that already ends with the signature line, keep the single line.
- Does not apply to Confluence comments — those follow their own intake format (`smartflow-feedback` Skill).
- Do not store repository- or project-specific values in this Rule.

## Source

Confluence Verbesserungsidee (SmartFlow feedback hub, page 1982857256); signature wording decided by the maintainer for release 1.5.0.
